{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000151","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"falcon-technique-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T11:56:13.020095+00:00","correlationId":"RF3","data":{"eventType":"claim.added","claim":{"id":"FTC1","statement":"Native Falcon Phase 1 (FalconHostSpooler.SpoolAsync) has no page-count stop. It follows the Discover after-token until the vendor terminal (after absent or empty string, normalised to null). It re-anchors in-process, never stops, in three cases: (a) proactively after MaxPagesPerCursorScroll pages on one cursor (default 500, clamp 1..100000), only when the page still has an after-token AND at least one fresh host carries last_seen; the stated reason is that server-side scroll context degrades with depth (hard 500 near page 1542), not cursor ageing; (b) FalconCursorExpiredException (404 on an after request; after-token TTL 120s); (c) HTTP status \u003E= 500, up to 5 consecutive (counter resets on any good page), after which the exception escapes and the host defers. A re-anchor issues a new query filtered last_seen_timestamp:\u003E= the watermark (whole second) or the base-date floor, with after=null, and resets the per-cursor page counter. The only other exits are 5 consecutive empty pages that still carry an after-token (truncation, see FTC6) and cancellation.","status":"open","evidenceIds":[],"consequenceIfWrong":"A YAML Phase-1 walk bounded by pagination.max_pages, or one without a re-anchor, cannot reproduce the native walk on large tenants.","provenance":{"actorId":"falcon-technique-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T11:56:13.020095+00:00","source":"claim.add"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000177","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"falcon-technique-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T11:57:19.103885+00:00","correlationId":"RF3","data":{"eventType":"claim.added","claim":{"id":"FTC6","statement":"The native manifest proves only that the Discover scroll ended, not that it was complete. When the spool stops with a live after-token (more than 5 consecutive empty pages), it logs at Error, still writes the manifest, and records the freeze as Degraded (units = stagedPages \u002B 1). Key collisions are recorded as unresolved and do not change the state. No caller reads the freeze state: a degraded freeze is reused like a complete one, Phase 2 publishes from it, and the run returns success. Native Falcon therefore does not fail a truncated freeze. PD2\u0027s rule (a store step that ends at max_pages fails the run) is stricter than native.","status":"open","evidenceIds":[],"consequenceIfWrong":"Whoever copies native behaviour literally keeps the silent-success path; PD2 should be recorded as a deliberate difference from native, not as parity.","provenance":{"actorId":"falcon-technique-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T11:57:19.103885+00:00","source":"claim.add"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000320","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"s3-contract-designer","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T15:07:49.669346+00:00","correlationId":"RD2","data":{"eventType":"decision.proposed","decision":{"id":"PD7","statement":"Re-anchor and truncation primitives (K13), opt-in on cursor-family pagination, one engine work item. New optional keys: cursor_recovery.reanchor_after_pages: N (after an accepted page, when pages since the last anchor \u003E= N, the next cursor is live and a watermark exists, re-anchor: drop the cursor, floor = watermark, reset the page counter; native FTC1a default 500); cursor_recovery.reanchor_on_status: [codes] with cursor_recovery.max_consecutive_reanchors: N (default 5; a classified response with a listed status re-anchors from the watermark, or the initial floor when none; the counter resets on any accepted page; past N the existing error handling decides; native FTC1c); pagination.empty_page_limit: N (N consecutive accepted pages with zero records while the cursor is live end the walk with stop reason truncated; native FTC6 uses 5). The existing expiry arm is unchanged. Re-anchor counters live in PaginationState and are never checkpointed. The loader rules for cursor_recovery (not on publishing stages or merge targets, not with prefetch) are unchanged, so store steps and merge sources are the only users.","status":"proposed","rationale":"K13 and K11 parity with the native spool (FTC1, FTC6). Reuses the one existing re-anchor action (PC10, PE4); no checkpoint change (PD8). Lesson L-76ed5c8b: the expiry arm stays unproven on the vendor (404 may arrive under 200).","dependsOnClaims":[],"provenance":{"actorId":"s3-contract-designer","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T15:07:49.669346+00:00","source":"decision.propose"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000337","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"falcon-docs-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:41:38.602685+00:00","correlationId":"RV1","data":{"eventType":"claim.added","claim":{"id":"FD1","statement":"CrowdStrike Discover combined hosts after tokens expire 120 seconds after a call is made.","status":"open","evidenceIds":[],"provenance":{"actorId":"falcon-docs-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:41:38.602685+00:00","source":"claim.add"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000340","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"falcon-docs-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:41:54.285915+00:00","correlationId":"RV1","data":{"eventType":"claim.added","claim":{"id":"FD2","statement":"CrowdStrike Spotlight vulnerability-management documentation says an expired after token is a 404 error code under errors in the response body, while the HTTP header is 200 OK.","status":"open","evidenceIds":[],"provenance":{"actorId":"falcon-docs-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:41:54.285915+00:00","source":"claim.add"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000343","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"falcon-docs-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:42:23.708652+00:00","correlationId":"RV1","data":{"eventType":"claim.added","claim":{"id":"FD3","statement":"The three repository CrowdStrike PDFs do not specify the HTTP status line or errors-body shape of an expired Discover combined-hosts after token, nor document scroll-depth failure near page 1542 or a re-anchor response to repeated 5xx.","status":"open","evidenceIds":[],"provenance":{"actorId":"falcon-docs-recon","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:42:23.708652+00:00","source":"claim.add"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000358","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"operator","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:47:41.758129+00:00","correlationId":"e53c5d0b063c42fb95e2271b4cd73062","data":{"eventType":"decision.resolved","decisionId":"PD7","status":"accepted"},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000366","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"s3-contract-designer","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:49:02.635406+00:00","correlationId":"RD4","data":{"eventType":"evidence.added","evidence":{"id":"PE10","sourceType":"source-read","citation":"yaml-adapter-engine origin/dev fa10015 src/Cymulate.Integration.Yaml.Engine/Resilience/Logic/EngineFailureClassifier.cs:21-42,273-297; Execution/Logic/Pages/PageLoop.cs:179-190","summary":"Roslyn source read: PageLoop passes HTTP status and response body to EngineFailureClassifier. IsExpiredCursor requires response.StatusCode == config.ExpiryStatus before searching expiry_message_contains in the body; with expiry_status 404, HTTP 200 carrying errors code 404 cannot reset to watermark and falls through rules/success classification.","supports":[],"refutes":["C6"],"provenance":{"actorId":"s3-contract-designer","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:49:02.635406+00:00","source":"evidence.add"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000368","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"s3-contract-designer","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:49:22.192848+00:00","correlationId":"RD4","data":{"eventType":"decision.proposed","decision":{"id":"PD10","statement":"Amend PD7 cursor-expiry detection for an opt-in cursor_recovery operation: retain the existing HTTP expiry_status plus expiry_message_contains arm, and also classify HTTP 200 as cursor expiry when response JSON has an errors[] entry whose code equals expiry_status (number or numeric string) and whose message matches expiry_message_contains case-insensitively. Both arms require an active after cursor and the existing watermark-available condition, run before generic success and error rules, and invoke the same ResetToWatermark action. Malformed JSON or an unrelated errors entry is not expiry. The proactive depth, listed-status 5xx, empty-page limit, counters, and no-checkpoint rule of PD7 remain; non-opt-in response handling is unchanged.","status":"proposed","rationale":"C6 rejected by PE10: EngineFailureClassifier.IsExpiredCursor at fa10015 gates on the HTTP status line, so Spotlight-documented HTTP 200 plus errors code 404 is missed. K11 and K22 require the Discover Phase-1 store walk to handle either shape without depending on undocumented Discover behavior (FD2, FD3). K21 confirms Phase 1 may restart from page 1 after crash, so no counter or watermark checkpoint is needed.","dependsOnClaims":[],"supersedes":"PD7","provenance":{"actorId":"s3-contract-designer","recordedAt":"2026-09-27T19:49:22.192848+00:00","source":"decision.propose"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
