{"schemaVersion":1,"eventId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write:0000000384","taskId":"2026-09-27_0827-yaml-engine-to-leverage-s3-read-and-write","actorId":"operator","recordedAt":"2026-09-28T07:22:05.491396+00:00","correlationId":"b79ccaa602284a8ba024a00f7ff0706a","data":{"eventType":"decision.proposed","decision":{"id":"D2","statement":"Scope split (coordinator proposal, 2026-09-28, awaiting operator choice). The scope is two tasks plus a later third. Task 1, engine re-anchor: PD7 and PD10, the pagination part of the phase-0 freeze (PaginationConfig, CursorRecoveryConfig, schema pagination keys), implement-falcon-reanchor, its tests and its engine release; it depends on nothing and delivers value alone (the Spotlight walk gains the body-404 expiry arm; any cursor walk gains depth and 5xx re-anchor). Task 2, stored sets engine plus host: PD4, PD5, PD6, PD8, PD9; the storage part of freeze-storage-and-reanchor-contracts, implement-stored-set-flow, engine storage tests, prepare-package-and-adapters-pin, implement-yamladapter-storage-host, test-yamladapter-storage-host; engine and host stay together because they are one capability through one frozen port and one assurance pair, and neither is usable alone. Task 3, later: the tactical Falcon YAML pilot update in integration-yaml (K15), after tasks 1 and 2 are released. Tasks 1 and 2 both change integration.schema.json and the pagination config, so whichever merges second rebases (same rule as PR #67, K20). If accepted: this task becomes task 2, OC1 is revised to remove the re-anchor item, and task 1 is opened with its own brief (constraints, PD7, PD10, evidence FD1-FD3, FTC1, FTC6, PE10 cited).","status":"proposed","rationale":"Re-anchor has disjoint files, its own failure class and its own release, and K13 already allows it to become its own task; shipping it separately delivers value earlier. Splitting stored sets from the host would add a handoff at the port and gain nothing. Option not chosen yet: keep one task and hand off OC1 as filed; it already works as a single task. Cost of the split: one planning run to revise OC1 plus opening task 1.","dependsOnClaims":[],"provenance":{"actorId":"operator","recordedAt":"2026-09-28T07:22:05.491396+00:00","source":"decision.propose"}}},"kernelIdentity":{"version":"2.0.157","sourceCommit":"b72437a","buildTime":"2026-09-24T17:12:52+00:00"}}
